+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Current voyage
+
+Greenfield bootstrap of a vanilla-JS TodoMVC app.
+
+Stack: HTML + CSS + vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors. Persistence via localStorage (`todos-vanilla`).
+Test runner: Cucumber with happy-dom. DOM-level scenarios under `features/`, step definitions under `features/support/`.
+Tooling: Biome for linting, Cypress (not yet installed) or manual browser verification for routing.
+
+Key decisions:
+- Flat directory structure: `js/app.js`, `css/app.css`, `index.html`
+- No framework, no build step
+- Flatiron Director not needed; use native `hashchange` for routing
+- localStorage key: `todos-vanilla`
diff --git a/features/add-and-edit-todos.feature b/features/add-and-edit-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3bbd87f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/add-and-edit-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+Feature: Add and edit todos
+  As a user
+  I want to add new todos and edit their titles
+  So that I can capture and refine my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Creating a new todo
+
+    Scenario: A new todo is added when the user presses Enter with non-empty text
+      When the user types "Buy milk" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+      And the new-todo input is empty
+
+    Scenario: Whitespace-only input does not create a todo
+      When the user types "   " in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+      And the new-todo input is empty
+
+    Scenario: The new-todo input is trimmed before creating a todo
+      When the user types "  Buy milk  " in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: The new-todo input is focused when the page loads
+      Then the new-todo input is focused
+
+  Rule: Editing an existing todo
+
+    Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label enters editing mode
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the label of the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo at position 1 has the "editing" class
+      And the edit input of the todo at position 1 contains "Buy milk"
+      And the edit input of the todo at position 1 is focused
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edit and exits editing mode
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And the todo at position 1 is in editing mode
+      When the user changes the edit input of the todo at position 1 to "Buy oat milk" and presses Enter
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy oat milk" and is not completed
+      And the todo at position 1 does not have the "editing" class
+
+    Scenario: Blurring the edit input saves the edit
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And the todo at position 1 is in editing mode
+      When the user changes the edit input of the todo at position 1 to "Buy oat milk" and blurs
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy oat milk" and is not completed
+      And the todo at position 1 does not have the "editing" class
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Escape discards changes and exits editing mode
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And the todo at position 1 is in editing mode
+      When the user changes the edit input of the todo at position 1 to "Buy oat milk" and presses Escape
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+      And the todo at position 1 does not have the "editing" class
+
+    Scenario: Saving an empty edit deletes the todo
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And the todo at position 1 is in editing mode
+      When the user clears the edit input of the todo at position 1 and presses Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+    Scenario: Saving a whitespace-only edit deletes the todo
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And the todo at position 1 is in editing mode
+      When the user changes the edit input of the todo at position 1 to "   " and presses Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
