@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+Feature: Delete a todo
+  As a user
+  I want to remove individual todos from my list
+  So that I can keep my list relevant
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Removing a todo
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the destroy button removes the todo
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user hovers over the todo at position 1
+      And the user clicks the destroy button of the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy eggs" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: The destroy button is not visible until hover
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      Then the destroy button of the todo at position 1 is not visible
+      When the user hovers over the todo at position 1
+      Then the destroy button of the todo at position 1 is visible
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..69f57f1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: localStorage persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to survive page reloads
+  So that I don't lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Data persistence
+
+    Scenario: Todos are persisted to localStorage after creation
+      When the user types "Buy milk" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      And the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Completed state is persisted to localStorage
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user clicks the toggle of the todo at position 1
+      And the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk" and is completed
+
+    Scenario: Deleted todos remain deleted after page reload
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user hovers over the todo at position 1
+      And the user clicks the destroy button of the todo at position 1
+      And the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy eggs" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: Editing a todo title is persisted to localStorage
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And the todo at position 1 is in editing mode
+      When the user changes the edit input of the todo at position 1 to "Buy oat milk" and presses Enter
+      And the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy oat milk" and is not completed
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1f5093d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Feature: Filtering by route
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todo list by All, Active, or Completed
+  So that I can focus on the tasks I care about
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Route-based filtering
+
+    Scenario: The default route shows all todos
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a completed todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then the todo list contains 2 items
+
+    Scenario: The #/active route shows only active todos
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a completed todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: The #/completed route shows only completed todos
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a completed todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      And the todo at position 1 has title "Buy eggs" and is completed
+
+    Scenario: The selected filter link is highlighted
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then the "Active" filter link is selected
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then the "Completed" filter link is selected
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then the "All" filter link is selected
+
+    Scenario: Toggling a todo while in a filtered view removes it from the list
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then the todo list contains 1 item
+      When the user clicks the toggle of the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo list contains 0 items
diff --git a/features/toggle-all.feature b/features/toggle-all.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..aafb76e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle-all.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+Feature: Toggle all todos
+  As a user
+  I want to mark all todos as complete or active in one action
+  So that I can manage my list efficiently
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the toggle-all checkbox marks all todos as completed
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk" and is completed
+      And the todo at position 2 has title "Buy eggs" and is completed
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the toggle-all checkbox when all are completed marks all as active
+      Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a completed todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+      And the todo at position 2 has title "Buy eggs" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: The toggle-all checkbox is checked when all todos are completed
+      Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a completed todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: The toggle-all checkbox is unchecked when some todos are active
+      Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
diff --git a/features/toggle-todo-state.feature b/features/toggle-todo-state.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dac77fd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/toggle-todo-state.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+Feature: Toggle todo completion state
+  As a user
+  I want to mark individual todos as complete or active
+  So that I can track which tasks are done
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Toggling a single todo
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the checkbox marks an active todo as completed
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user clicks the toggle of the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk" and is completed
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the checkbox of a completed todo marks it as active
+      Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user clicks the toggle of the todo at position 1
+      Then the todo at position 1 has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+
+    Scenario: The toggle-all checkbox state reflects individual todo states
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      When the user clicks the toggle of the todo at position 1
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
+      When the user clicks the toggle of the todo at position 2
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
diff --git a/features/ui-state.feature b/features/ui-state.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9c6a2ee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/ui-state.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+Feature: UI state management
+  As a user
+  I want the app to show and hide sections appropriately
+  So that the interface stays clean and relevant
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Conditional visibility
+
+    Scenario: The main section and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+      Then the main section is hidden
+      And the footer is hidden
+
+    Scenario: The main section and footer are visible when there are todos
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      Then the main section is visible
+      And the footer is visible
+
+    Scenario: The item counter shows the number of active todos
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a completed todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      Then the item counter shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: The item counter uses plural form for multiple active todos
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And a todo "Buy eggs" exists
+      Then the item counter shows "2 items left"
+
+    Scenario: The item counter shows zero items left
+      Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      Then the item counter shows "0 items left"
